@startuml c4-activity
' DOC-9. C4, fault tolerance: what a process does with a run that a crash left unfinished.
' Card: docs/algorithms/C4.md#pseudocode
' code: flowstat.recovery.wal:WriteAheadLog.commit
' code: flowstat.engine.scheduler:Scheduler.restore
' code: flowstat.engine.scheduler:Scheduler.resolve
' code: flowstat.recovery.saga:compensation_blockers
skinparam shadowing false

start
:commit: store the events that are not stored yet,\nin one transaction, before any command runs;
note right: this is what a crash leaves behind
:restore(history, now, idempotent);
:fold the events: states, outputs, attempts;
if (the run has an outcome?) then (yes)
  :nothing to do;
  stop
endif
:log RUN_RESUMED;
:counters, stopped, cancelled, compensate_requested\nread from the recorded states;
if (stopped and not undoing?) then (yes)
  :cancel everything that is not terminal\n(completes a partial stop);
endif
partition "for every step that was RUNNING or COMPENSATING" {
  if (idempotent(its action)?) then (yes)
    :command Start with the same attempt (same key);
  else (no)
    :state UNCERTAIN, log STEP_UNCERTAIN (E-REC-001);
  endif
}
if (undoing?) then (yes)
  :blockers: rebuild from the states\n(bitset of descendants, reverse topological order);
  :dispatch the undo calls that are ready;
else (no)
  :queue every PENDING step without an unfinished predecessor;
  :advance the scheduler;
endif
:WAITING stays WAITING; UNCERTAIN stays UNCERTAIN;
if (a person decides about an UNCERTAIN step?) then (resolve)
  if (decision) then (done)
    :log STEP_RESOLVED; finish the step\n(an undo becomes COMPENSATED);
  else (retry)
    :attempt + 1; log STEP_RESOLVED; command Start;
  endif
endif
stop
@enduml
